                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 18 at 5:08PM MDT until September 18 at 8:15PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "FFWABQ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Albuquerque has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSouth Central Lincoln County in central New Mexico...\n\n* Until 815 PM MDT.\n\n* At 508 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 0.75 and 1.5 inches of\nrain have fallen along the Lincoln and Otero County line north of\nWhitetail. Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.5 inches are\npossible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nGlencoe.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
